innova2-app (1.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * innova2-smi ddr (and a "DDR speed" line in status): DDR calibration and
    mode, the build's MIG parameters (part, tCK, MT/s, CL/CWL, tRCD/tRP/tRAS/
    tRFC, width, ECC, InputClockPeriod, CA drive, POLL_CYC) from a per-build
    table keyed by ROM_TS (read from each build's MIG RTL / IP parameters /
    par XDC / CA-drive gate / create_project log), the MIG ui_clk measured
    passively from the ECC poll count and the 250 MHz uptime counter
    (MT/s = 8 x ui_clk, 4:1 PHY; +-0.2 % over 1.5 s), and the ECC totals.
  * check: ddr.rate_mismatch (WARN, > 1 % off the table), ddr.rate_unverified
    (INFO: unlisted build, or route V whose MIG comes with each xclbin).
  * A hook (DDR_INFO_MAPS) for route V's planned DDR_INFO register block.
  * docs/innova2_smi_regmap.md lists the MIG table.

 -- Michal Kouril <xmkouril@gmail.com>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 23:30:00 -0400

innova2-app (1.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * innova2-smi memory, and a memory section in status / status --json: every
    memory bank of the loaded xclbin (tag, type, base, size, used, the CU
    arguments on it, ready, prune state), read passively from xocl's sysfs
    mem_topology / ip_layout / connectivity (no XRT context, no xrt-smi).
    PRUNED is shown only where verifiable (route V's DDR, from RV_INFO);
    unused PLRAM/HOST/PEER banks are "unused (may be pruned)".
  * check: mem.no_xclbin (INFO), mem.bank_not_ready (FAIL: a used bank that
    is not calibrated / ready), mem.ddr_kept_not_ready (WARN, route V: DDR
    KEPT while ddr_ready=0), identity.vpd_empty (WARN).
  * list / status: a ConnectX-5 with an empty VPD (hpz440's card) prints
    "VPD empty" and its PSID / firmware instead of "serial ? board ? rev ?",
    and is no longer called "NOT a validated board" (it cannot be checked).
  * docs/innova2_smi_prune_marker.md: proposed xclbin marker for the hooks.

 -- Michal Kouril <xmkouril@gmail.com>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 22:30:00 -0400

innova2-app (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New command innova2-smi: query and test the Innova-2 XRT shell (fp8c
    lineage: E6b, E6b-2400, E7a2, E7a3, E7a3-2666ca48). list, status, check
    (passive, exit 0/1/2), counters (--watch), recorder, clear, ddr-mode,
    throttle (including simulate-hot / restore) and test (validate, p2p,
    ddr-soak, temp-live, ecc-live, throttle, pr-stress, flash-verify).
  * Cards are found from the ConnectX-5 side and the FPGA state is classified
    (shell, Flex, missing, other design, unreadable) before any register read.
  * Every register access goes through the running shell's OBS_ID register map
    (docs/innova2_smi_regmap.md); an unknown shell is refused.
  * innova2_app is unchanged.

 -- Michal Kouril <xmkouril@gmail.com>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0400

innova2-app (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First Debian packaging: innova2-app (the app) and innova2-areg-dkms
    (the innova2_areg kernel module, built by DKMS for every installed
    kernel that has headers).
  * --transport kmod replaces --transport node (still accepted).
  * The burn read-back scratch file goes to /var/lib/innova2-app when it
    exists.
  * build.sh leaves the module alone when innova2-areg-dkms manages it.
  * README: reorganised; mlx5_fpga_tools was removed in MLNX_OFED 5.3.

 -- Michal Kouril <xmkouril@gmail.com>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 13:15:06 -0400
